  "id": "pain-drawing",
  "term": "pain drawing",
  "definition": "A pain drawing is a simple tool used during history-taking in which a patient shows or marks their pain to help communication with a clinician. In mental health-related assessment of back pain, it has been studied as a possible screening aid for signs of anxiety, depression, and reduced quality of life.",
